/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# The calendar feed (/cleanups.ics, built by src/pages/cleanups.ics.ts).
# Pages infers a type from the extension, but not reliably the charset — and the
# feed is full of multi-byte characters (an em dash in every event name). The
# nosniff above means whatever type is sent is the type the client is stuck with,
# so say it here. This is also the ONLY lever: a static build writes the
# endpoint's body to disk and throws its Response headers away.
# One block, not a second Content-Type on /* — Cloudflare comma-joins duplicate
# header values, which would produce a nonsense type.
/cleanups.ics
  Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8
